abstract: >-
  Interactive universe sandbox: a full-screen living universe where you play
  god. Tap to birth a star, drag to tear open a black hole (it pulls nearby
  stars into orbit and swallows the ones that fall in), detonate a supernova
  into a nebula, or spin up a whole spiral galaxy. Presets: Big Bang, Milky
  Way, Black Hole, Nebula. Controls for time speed, gravity, star count and
  a scale slider that zooms from quantum foam out to galaxy clusters; a
  Quantum field toggle reveals flowing wave lines beneath everything, a nod
  to Faggin's quantum-field view of the universe. A playful simulation, not
  real astrophysics: gravity and orbits are simplified for fun, and the
  displayed entropy is a game quantity, not a thermodynamic measurement. The
  quantum-field view is a visual motif, not a measurement. No DOI yet (no
  Zenodo record).
